---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
---

<Layout
  title="Repeater Map | Aegis-Beacon"
  description="Interactive map of amateur radio repeaters around you. Live data from OpenStreetMap and verified database, no API key required."
>
  <div class="repeaters-page container">
    <header class="section-head" style="padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);">
      <h1 class="section-head__title">Repeater Map</h1>
      <p class="section-head__lead">
        Find amateur radio repeaters around you to relay voice traffic while an Aegis-Beacon
        transmits. The map integrates verified repeater directories and live OpenStreetMap data.
        Search by city, mountain, or callsign, or click &ldquo;Repeaters near me&rdquo;.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="repeaters-layout">
      <div class="repeaters-toolbar" data-rv>
        <div class="repeaters-toolbar__actions">
          <button id="locate-btn" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 2v3M12 19v3M2 12h3M19 12h3"/></svg>
            Repeaters near me
          </button>
          <button id="reload-btn" class="btn btn-secondary" type="button">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 11-2.64-6.36"/><path d="M21 3v6h-6"/></svg>
            Search this area
          </button>
        </div>

        <form id="search-form" class="repeaters-search-box" onsubmit="return false;">
          <input
            type="search"
            id="city-search"
            class="repeaters-search-input"
            placeholder="City, mountain or callsign (e.g. Roma, Milano, IR0A)..."
            aria-label="Search city, mountain or callsign"
          />
          <button id="city-search-btn" class="btn btn-secondary" type="submit">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"/><path d="M21 21l-4.35-4.35"/></svg>
            Search
          </button>
        </form>

        <div class="repeaters-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter by band">
          <button class="repeaters-filter is-active" data-band="all" type="button">All bands</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="2m" type="button">2 m</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="70cm" type="button">70 cm</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="6m" type="button">6 m</button>
          <button class="repeaters-filter" data-band="23cm" type="button">23 cm</button>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-status" id="repeaters-status" role="status">
          Loading repeaters...
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="repeaters-map-wrap" data-rv style="--rv-delay: 120ms">
        <div id="repeaters-map" class="repeaters-map" aria-label="Map of amateur radio repeaters"></div>
        <div class="repeaters-map-note">
          Map &copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap</a>
          contributors &middot; repeater data &copy; OpenStreetMap (ODbL) and verified community directory
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="repeaters-results" data-rv style="--rv-delay: 200ms">
        <div class="repeaters-results__head">
          <h2>Repeaters found</h2>
          <span class="repeaters-count" id="repeaters-count">0</span>
        </div>
        <p class="repeaters-results__lead">
          Select any repeater from the list to center it on the map and view transmit frequencies, CTCSS sub-tones and offsets.
        </p>
        <div class="repeaters-list" id="repeaters-list"></div>
        <div class="repeaters-empty" id="repeaters-empty" hidden>
          <p><strong>No repeaters found in this immediate view.</strong></p>
          <p>
            Try zooming out or searching for a nearby city in the search bar above.
            You can also consult external directories:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="https://www.repeaterbook.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RepeaterBook</a>, worldwide amateur radio directory</li>
            <li><a href="https://repeatermap.de/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RepeaterMap</a>, community ham radio map</li>
            <li><a href="https://repeater.oevsv.at/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OEVSV repeater map</a>, Austria</li>
            <li><a href="https://www.uska.ch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USKA</a>, Switzerland</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="repeaters-faq">
      <h2>How to use this with the beacon</h2>
      <div class="repeaters-faq__grid">
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Why repeaters?</h3>
          <p>
            The Aegis-Beacon itself transmits simplex Morse on 433 MHz and never needs a repeater. Repeaters
            matter to the people <em>listening</em>: a voice relay on 2 m or 70 cm extends the radius in which
            a rescue coordinator or mountain guide can acknowledge the beacon and organize a response.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Offsets and tones</h3>
          <p>
            European repeaters use standard offsets (2 m: -600 kHz, 70 cm: -1.6 MHz or -7.6 MHz) and often
            require a CTCSS tone on the uplink. Always confirm tone and offset on RepeaterBook before a trip,
            and make a simplex fallback plan in case the machine is off.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Privacy</h3>
          <p>
            Your position is read with the browser geolocation API and never leaves the device. Only the map
            area you look at is sent to OpenStreetMap and Overpass to load tiles and repeaters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="repeaters-card">
          <h3>Related docs</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/wiki/frequency-compatibility">Frequency table and legal limits</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/receiver-compatibility">What receivers can hear</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/sdr-listening-guide">Listening with an SDR</a></li>
            <li><a href="/wiki/regulatory-compliance">Operating legally</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

